"""
verify-code v2.3 — grab codes, find events, track subscriptions, add to calendar.

Modes:
  verify-code setup            Interactive wizard: credentials + Google Calendar OAuth.
  verify-code                  One-shot: copy newest verification code from last 10 min.
  verify-code daemon           Background: watch inbox, auto-copy codes, extract events.
  verify-code install          Install auto-start service for login.
  verify-code scan             Scan inbox for events with dates/times (no code copy).
  verify-code subscriptions    View all tracked subscriptions with warnings and spending totals.
  verify-code dashboard        Launch a web dashboard in your browser.
  verify-code auth             (Re-)authenticate Google Calendar.
  verify-code version          Show the installed version.
  verify-code --version        Show the installed version (alternative).
  verify-code history          Show the last 10 copied verification codes.

Features:
  - Gmail, Outlook, and Hotmail IMAP support
  - Subscription tracking: detect plans, renewals, trials from 80+ services
  - Free trial warnings and renewal reminders
  - Secure Mode: auto-erase clipboard after N seconds
  - BODY.PEEK so messages are NEVER marked read.
  - IMAP IDLE for instant delivery (falls back to polling).
  - Known-sender whitelist (80+ senders) prevents false positives.
  - Confidence scoring for code extraction.
  - Dedup tracking — codes never re-copied, events never re-added.
  - Atomic state writes with CRC validation.
  - Credentials in ~/.config/verify-code/ (chmod 600).
  - OAuth token stored alongside credentials.
"""

